Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.07,0:00:24.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[uptempo classical tune playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.66,0:00:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gunshot]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.51,0:00:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[uptempo tune continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.02,0:00:55.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pull!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.05,0:01:28.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tempo slows]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.72,0:01:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[pigeon coos]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.43,0:01:37.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tempo increases]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.57,0:01:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[piano music intensifies]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.03,0:01:53.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[neck cracks]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.54,0:01:57.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crows cawing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.79,0:01:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.00,0:02:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chews loudly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.55,0:02:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.47,0:02:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you please ask Miss Nolan{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.18,0:02:13.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if my personal effects{\i0}\N{\i1}have yet been removed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.60,0:02:16.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}from the duke's bedchamber{\i0}\N{\i1}and placed in the duchess's rooms?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.06,0:02:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you please inform Her Grace{\i0}\N{\i1}that I will allow no such thing?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.23,0:02:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I really deliver the message,{\i0}\N{\i1}Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.86,0:02:29.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You cannot believe{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall welcome you back into my bed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.15,0:02:30.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}after your lies and deception?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.78,0:02:31.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] Rest assured,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.82,0:02:33.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}marital relations{\i0}\N{\i1}are the least of my concern{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.99,0:02:35.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}after your recent efforts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.33,0:02:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then for what other purpose{\i0}\N{\i1}could you possibly wish to detain me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.16,0:02:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[slams chalice] Because you are my wife.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.87,0:02:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne slams chalice]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.88,0:02:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is customary for a wife{\i0}\N{\i1}to reside in her own bedchamber{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.63,0:02:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}once the honeymoon is over…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.34,0:02:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}a time that has well and truly passed,{\i0}\N{\i1}would you not agree?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.01,0:02:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will be kept informed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.72,0:02:57.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as to the success{\i0}\N{\i1}of your conjugal endeavors.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.85,0:03:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would never dream of concealing{\i0}\N{\i1}the truth of such important matters.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.56,0:03:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[door opens]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your Grace, Whistledown has just arrived.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.32,0:03:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Well, you should…{\i0}\N{\i1}-Is something wrong?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.82,0:03:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-We must pack straightaway.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.82,0:03:12.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What has happened?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.12,0:03:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My brother seems{\i0}\N{\i1}to have been embroiled in scandal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.87,0:03:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must return to my family immediately.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.45,0:03:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-They will need me.{\i0}\N{\i1}-I will accompany you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.50,0:03:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is a family matter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.04,0:03:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Separate bedrooms may be tolerated.{\i0}\N{\i1}Separate households will not be suffered.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.25,0:03:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll not let you out of my sight{\i0}\N{\i1}until we know whether you are with child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.92,0:03:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[scoffing chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.26,0:03:35.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please request that His Grace{\i0}\N{\i1}prepare his largest carriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.60,0:03:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall require my space.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.31,0:03:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.60,0:03:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[intense music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.36,0:03:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[overlapping chatter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.41,0:03:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown] {\i0}<span style="style2">Miss Marina Thompson's{\i0}\N<span style="style2">{\an8}recent fall from grace{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.66,0:04:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}continues to echo{\i0}\N{\i1}through every drawing room in town,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.91,0:04:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}days after it was revealed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.42,0:04:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}her engagement to Colin Bridgerton{\i0}\N{\i1}was nothing more than a sham.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.18,0:04:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course, a lady's disgrace{\i0}\N{\i1}does not merely tarnish her own name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.60,0:04:23.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like the tars of the Thames,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.56,0:04:27.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}it also leaves a horrid smear{\i0}\N{\i1}on anyone nearby.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.48,0:04:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hold still, {\i0}<span style="style2">ma chérie{\i0}{\i1}.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.86,0:04:35.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This scandal could very well{\i0}\N{\i1}tarnish my debut, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.78,0:04:38.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps we should delay my coming out{\i0}\N{\i1}altogether a few years.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.32,0:04:41.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hush, child, all will be well.{\i0}\N{\i1}Just keep smiling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.16,0:04:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise] Can a smile be enough{\i0}\N{\i1}to save the Featheringtons?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.58,0:04:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Penelope and her sisters{\i0}\N{\i1}did nothing wrong,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.08,0:04:46.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but their reputation's destroyed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.67,0:04:49.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should be worrying about{\i0}\N{\i1}your own family's fortunes at present.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.50,0:04:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We are in just as perilous position.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.80,0:04:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lovely day, is it not, Lady Richmond?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.09,0:04:58.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's this Whistledown.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.30,0:05:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I certainly never want to cross the woman.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.64,0:05:02.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her word as good as gospel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.64,0:05:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.60,0:05:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, perhaps{\i0}\N{\i1}if she can destroy a reputation…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.81,0:05:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}she can restore one too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.65,0:05:14.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps theatrically]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Très élégante, {\i0}{\i1}Miss Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.07,0:05:17.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What a debutante you will be!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.28,0:05:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.20,0:05:20.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">While there is no parasol in the world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.74,0:05:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}strong enough to shelter a ruined woman,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.70,0:05:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the fallen Miss Thompson can only hope{\i0}\N{\i1}she shall find a refuge{\i0}<span style="style1">…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.00,0:05:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}somewhere.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.21,0:05:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I am sorry, my lady, but we are full.{\i0}\N{\i1}-This is an emergency.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.80,0:05:35.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The young lady's child{\i0}\N{\i1}will have nowhere else to go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.47,0:05:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must make exceptions on occasion?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.88,0:05:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should be able to procure a room{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.72,0:05:41.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if one were to make a sizable donation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.80,0:05:44.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Featherington] But this is supposed to be{\i0}\N{\i1}a charitable organization.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.97,0:05:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[nurse] Even charity requires funds,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.64,0:05:49.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of which you must have{\i0}\N{\i1}considerable amounts, I presume?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.77,0:05:51.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… [sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.91,0:06:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[horse neighs]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[driver] Whoa there, boy. Whoa there!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.21,0:06:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have arrived.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.80,0:06:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is no need to act the jailer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.17,0:06:21.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall not discover I am with child{\i0}\N{\i1}within the next hour, shall I?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.39,0:06:28.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson must be in agonies{\i0}\N{\i1}over these lies. Why can I not visit her?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.48,0:06:30.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Colin--{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Anthony] Listen to me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.10,0:06:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That the ton devours{\i0}\N{\i1}every bit of Whistledown's on-dit{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.61,0:06:34.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is the only thing{\i0}\N{\i1}keeping this family from shame.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.57,0:06:35.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because of her, no one believes{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.98,0:06:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you are the father{\i0}\N{\i1}of Miss Thompson's child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.03,0:06:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But if you were to go near her,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.53,0:06:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}they'll presume you responsible{\i0}\N{\i1}for her ruin,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.45,0:06:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and your sisters{\i0}\N{\i1}will pay the price for your notoriety.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.62,0:06:45.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Is this what you desire?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Of course not, but--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.66,0:06:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Evening, everyone.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Dearest!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.04,0:06:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are you doing here?{\i0}\N{\i1}Should you not be frolicking{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.29,0:06:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in newlywed bliss?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.33,0:06:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I came as swiftly as our carriage{\i0}\N{\i1}would allow when I heard the news.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.09,0:06:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In the middle of your honeymoon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.46,0:06:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hastings must surely be cursing{\i0}\N{\i1}the Bridgerton name for this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.17,0:06:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where is he, anyhow?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.55,0:07:01.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He went to set up Hastings House.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.38,0:07:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have all things in order, Sister.{\i0}\N{\i1}We do not require your assistance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.14,0:07:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is simply not true, and you know it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.01,0:07:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne may be{\i0}\N{\i1}the answer to all of our problems.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.27,0:07:12.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Once the ton see that we still have{\i0}\N{\i1}the favor of the duke and duchess,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.15,0:07:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}then the whispers may very well cease,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.56,0:07:17.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and we shall go about our daily lives{\i0}\N{\i1}as if nothing has happened,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.94,0:07:18.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as if nothing is awry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.03,0:07:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And no one will be the wiser.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.20,0:07:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pretending that nothing is amiss{\i0}\N{\i1}is the perfect way{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.32,0:07:27.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to lure the ignorant into submission.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.91,0:07:29.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it not, Mama?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.46,0:07:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, what grand event{\i0}\N{\i1}will the ton be descending upon this week?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.09,0:07:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely there is something?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.09,0:07:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[clears throat] The, um…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.17,0:07:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The queen is hosting a luncheon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.88,0:07:44.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am certain{\i0}\N{\i1}the duke and I can secure an invitation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.55,0:07:45.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If we are lucky,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.60,0:07:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}our return to London will give everyone{\i0}\N{\i1}so much to talk about,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.35,0:07:51.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}they simply have no breath left{\i0}\N{\i1}to discuss other matters.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.93,0:07:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm so very glad{\i0}\N{\i1}this has all been settled on my behalf.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.40,0:07:57.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door slams]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.73,0:08:00.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[knocking on door]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.91,0:08:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] You really wanted to marry her?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.41,0:08:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.41,0:08:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, then,{\i0}\N{\i1}perhaps we should count you lucky{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.08,0:08:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to not have married a stranger.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.71,0:08:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-She was not a stranger.{\i0}\N{\i1}-She {\i0}<span style="style2">was,{\i0}{\i1} Brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.71,0:08:22.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Whistledown knew her better than you.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Whistledown knows everyone's secrets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.88,0:08:24.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're lucky{\i0}\N{\i1}to have learned Miss Thompson's now,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.93,0:08:26.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}instead of after your wedding day.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.18,0:08:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know you must think me a fool…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.19,0:08:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but my heart pays no heed to mere logic.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.06,0:08:38.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When I think of her,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.07,0:08:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I only want to be near her,{\i0}\N{\i1}to be with her…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.65,0:08:44.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}despite all reason otherwise.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.70,0:08:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know that madness well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.99,0:08:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but you cannot visit her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.46,0:09:01.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Leander swam Abydos to Sestos{\i0}\N{\i1}every single night in complete darkness{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.92,0:09:03.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}just to see his love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.21,0:09:06.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Leander also lost his way and drowned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.18,0:09:10.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So the story goes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.35,0:09:14.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did something happen, Sister,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.56,0:09:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}back at Clyvedon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.02,0:09:20.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.23,0:09:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you really must speak{\i0}\N{\i1}with Miss Thompson,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.57,0:09:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}perhaps I can arrange a rendezvous.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.15,0:09:26.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Chaperoned, obviously.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.95,0:09:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would appreciate that.{\i0}\N{\i1}You will see my passions are not in vain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.08,0:09:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting, groaning]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.42,0:09:42.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Always were a fast learner, friend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.92,0:09:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I should probably conserve my energies{\i0}\N{\i1}for my exhibitions,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.55,0:09:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}instead of spending them on your troubles.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.51,0:09:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you about to cede to me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.30,0:09:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely that will not help{\i0}\N{\i1}with your exhibitions?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.72,0:09:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've not seen you this incensed{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.22,0:09:56.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}since you were handed the keys{\i0}\N{\i1}to your dukedom.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.10,0:10:00.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I will not speak of my dukedom.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[chuckles] Fair enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.35,0:10:03.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I presume you won't speak of what happened{\i0}\N{\i1}on your honeymoon, either.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.27,0:10:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nothing happened on my honeymoon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.65,0:10:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I cannot imagine your wife feeling{\i0}\N{\i1}particularly excited about that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.61,0:10:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suggest you do not try to imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}anything to do with my wife's feelings…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.03,0:10:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or actions, for that matter. [grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.37,0:10:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.62,0:10:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It follows no reason or sense, does it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.21,0:10:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-What?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.71,0:10:24.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And there is not a bloody thing{\i0}\N{\i1}you can do about it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.63,0:10:27.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I took a vow.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Ah.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.17,0:10:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}See what I mean?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.05,0:10:31.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fast learner, indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.51,0:10:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.98,0:10:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.44,0:10:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sighs deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.82,0:10:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[footsteps approaching]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.07,0:10:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.12,0:11:02.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon] You are still awake?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.42,0:11:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have already seen you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.84,0:11:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The queen is holding a luncheon this week.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.68,0:11:18.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We will need to attend with my brother{\i0}\N{\i1}to signal our support.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.94,0:11:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where have you been all night?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.40,0:11:25.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not think you concerned{\i0}\N{\i1}about my whereabouts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.15,0:11:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is this truly{\i0}\N{\i1}what our marriage will be for the future?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.32,0:11:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You out all night, doing God knows what{\i0}\N{\i1}with God knows whom?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.24,0:11:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"With whom?"{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.78,0:11:34.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You wound me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.24,0:11:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not three weeks since we were wed,{\i0}\N{\i1}yet already you imagine me disloyal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.49,0:11:40.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it such a wild imagining?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.46,0:11:43.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We both know your reputation, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.67,0:11:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is clear that you find{\i0}\N{\i1}there is nothing left in our marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.29,0:11:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nothing left?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.30,0:11:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is what I said.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.05,0:11:53.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it what you believe?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.15,0:12:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne moans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.99,0:12:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.61,0:12:17.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Simon.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Daphne.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.83,0:12:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I want you--{\i0}\N{\i1}-Shh.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.96,0:12:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne moans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.22,0:12:36.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.56,0:12:41.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.27,0:12:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne grunting, panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.65,0:12:53.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.57,0:12:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.33,0:13:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should we go into the bedroom…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.37,0:13:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and finish what we started?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.92,0:13:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.47,0:13:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is to become of us? Simon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.18,0:13:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are with child, then I shall stay{\i0}\N{\i1}and do my duty to support you both.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.48,0:13:25.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And if I am not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.60,0:13:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then we shall remain married{\i0}\N{\i1}in name only.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.27,0:13:29.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasps]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.19,0:13:32.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will be provided for, of course,{\i0}\N{\i1}in a manner befitting the duchess.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.15,0:13:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I shall not{\i0}\N{\i1}darken your doorstep again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.90,0:13:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our lives will be entirely separate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.16,0:13:38.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.66,0:13:40.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This cannot happen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.33,0:13:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This will not happen.{\i0}\N{\i1}Do you understand me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.33,0:13:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That we no longer trust each other?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.12,0:13:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.58,0:13:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I understand that quite well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.30,0:13:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door slams]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.90,0:14:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.61,0:14:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.61,0:14:20.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.49,0:14:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you for joining us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.99,0:14:25.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not realize I had a choice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.58,0:14:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My brother wished for an audience.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.96,0:14:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I wish to avoid any further scandal{\i0}\N{\i1}attached to my family's name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.34,0:14:35.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I will remain here as a chaperone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.88,0:14:41.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina… you must tell me{\i0}\N{\i1}that this Whistledown woman is mistaken.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.22,0:14:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What she wrote, it cannot be true.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.43,0:14:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it is.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.60,0:14:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are with child?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.77,0:14:51.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.94,0:14:55.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We were to be wed.{\i0}\N{\i1}You… You said you loved me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.36,0:14:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Colin, I hold you in the greatest esteem.{\i0}\N{\i1}-"Esteem"?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.94,0:15:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are a cruel woman indeed to stand here{\i0}\N{\i1}and talk of friendly affection,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.32,0:15:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as if you have not just committed{\i0}\N{\i1}a grave sin against me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.95,0:15:07.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Speak not of sin, Mr. Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.33,0:15:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not come here{\i0}\N{\i1}to be shamed by you, nor anyone else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.01,0:15:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did not know better.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.05,0:15:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You may think me a villain,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I did what I thought I must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.60,0:15:30.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No one ever truly helped me,{\i0}\N{\i1}or guided me in a different direction.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.77,0:15:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had no choice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.60,0:15:35.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I needed to wed.{\i0}\N{\i1}And you, you were the only man{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.40,0:15:37.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}who offered me{\i0}\N{\i1}even a glimpse of happiness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.65,0:15:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So I should feel flattered, then?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.44,0:15:42.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Consider myself lucky that you chose me,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.03,0:15:45.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}lied to me, tried to trick me{\i0}\N{\i1}into a fraud of a marriage?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.87,0:15:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall take my leave of you{\i0}\N{\i1}for the last time, Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.68,0:16:13.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You wish to know{\i0}\N{\i1}the cruelest part of your deception?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.85,0:16:17.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you had simply come to me{\i0}\N{\i1}and told me of your situation…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.77,0:16:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'd have married you{\i0}\N{\i1}without a second thought.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.99,0:16:24.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That is how in love{\i0}\N{\i1}I believed myself to be.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.87,0:16:29.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I see now that was all a lie.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.04,0:16:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door slams]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.88,0:16:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.88,0:16:43.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe I would like to return home now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.76,0:16:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After all, we don't want another scandal{\i0}\N{\i1}attached to your family name.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.01,0:16:51.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.64,0:16:57.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The carriage is waiting, ma'am.{\i0}\N{\i1}We must prepare for the queen's luncheon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.06,0:16:58.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.23,0:17:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[violin quintet playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.90,0:17:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.00,0:17:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, is this not lovely?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.92,0:17:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All of us together again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.01,0:17:27.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lovely, indeed.{\i0}\N{\i1}We should tempt scandal more often.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.72,0:17:35.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Duchess, may I say how well you look?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh, you are too kind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.48,0:17:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is it not marvelous to be wed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.39,0:17:39.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is both a joy and a wonder indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.23,0:17:41.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Queen Charlotte] Make way!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.69,0:17:44.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Must you all act{\i0}\N{\i1}like sheep flocking to the trough?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.99,0:17:47.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have 100 guineas wagered{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.61,0:17:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}on there being a Hastings heir{\i0}\N{\i1}within the year.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.03,0:17:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you yet with child?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.41,0:17:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have certainly been{\i0}\N{\i1}devoting our energies{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.58,0:17:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to the endeavor, Your Majesty.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.29,0:17:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We should hope{\i0}\N{\i1}to see our queen soon satisfied.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.29,0:17:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}See to it that you do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.09,0:18:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your duplicity comes so naturally.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.42,0:18:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I seem to have learned from the best.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.39,0:18:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've missed you at the studio of late.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.26,0:18:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must join me{\i0}\N{\i1}for another drawing lesson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.43,0:18:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As I said,{\i0}\N{\i1}improvement is all a matter of practice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.19,0:18:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At least, that is the excuse he gives{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.27,0:18:23.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for coming home with paint{\i0}\N{\i1}in all kinds of peculiar places.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.69,0:18:25.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[giggles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Henry chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.82,0:18:28.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Henry] Ah!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.74,0:18:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Were you able to meet{\i0}\N{\i1}my friend Wetherby at my party?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.57,0:18:34.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Come, I shall introduce you.{\i0}\N{\i1}-No, thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.91,0:18:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I-- I see my mother requires my presence.{\i0}\N{\i1}Good day!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.71,0:18:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her Majesty requires an audience.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.75,0:18:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}With-- With me? Now?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.09,0:18:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah. Here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.72,0:18:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[dog barking]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.84,0:18:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shoo.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.19,0:19:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who is she?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.81,0:19:03.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Majesty?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.77,0:19:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Whistledown!{\i0}\N{\i1}-Oh.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.90,0:19:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I tasked you{\i0}\N{\i1}with unmasking the scandalmonger.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.23,0:19:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Believe me, I am intent on locating her{\i0}\N{\i1}and am angry at myself{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.95,0:19:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for having not yet uncovered her identity.{\i0}\N{\i1}But I was thinking--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.87,0:19:15.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Clearly not fast enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.24,0:19:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My patience has limits.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.99,0:19:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Mm.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Get me an answer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.66,0:19:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your queen commands it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.08,0:19:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.13,0:19:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Majesty. [clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.13,0:19:29.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, you have returned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.63,0:19:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Excellent timing,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.68,0:19:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}what with all the tittle-tattle{\i0}\N{\i1}concerning your brother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.89,0:19:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, a mere coincidence,{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Danbury, I am sure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.81,0:19:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm. Your plan is working.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.31,0:19:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have heard nary a peep{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.06,0:19:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}about Mr. Bridgerton's{\i0}\N{\i1}unfortunate entanglement{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.56,0:19:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with the Thompson girl.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.77,0:19:47.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, I almost forgot.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.48,0:19:50.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am hosting a party{\i0}\N{\i1}I would very much like you to attend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.94,0:19:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We love a good party.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.78,0:19:56.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not sure{\i0}\N{\i1}when we will be accepting invitations.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.74,0:19:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is an invitation for one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.16,0:20:01.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only you, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.46,0:20:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A special soiree{\i0}\N{\i1}with the married ladies of the ton,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.96,0:20:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of which you are the newest member.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.76,0:20:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inaudible murmuring]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.10,0:20:27.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The audacity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.32,0:20:31.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}After they tried{\i0}\N{\i1}to entrap poor Mr. Bridgerton{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.86,0:20:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}into marriage with a woman with child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.86,0:20:34.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Cowper scoffs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.20,0:20:39.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.54,0:20:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How are you faring?{\i0}\N{\i1}Has it been terrible at the house?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.67,0:20:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've not had a caller in three days.{\i0}\N{\i1}My mother swears we are ruined.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.88,0:20:53.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But what of Colin?{\i0}\N{\i1}Is he in pieces from the news?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.84,0:20:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His pride is wounded,{\i0}\N{\i1}but he will be quite well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.05,0:20:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The gentlemen always are{\i0}\N{\i1}in these matters, but…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.55,0:21:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pen, you have not heard{\i0}\N{\i1}what people are saying.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.64,0:21:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown{\i0}\N{\i1}has gone too far this time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.93,0:21:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I thought you her greatest admirer.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.52,0:21:07.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not when she has smeared{\i0}\N{\i1}the name of my greatest friend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.85,0:21:09.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When we uncover Whistledown's identity,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.48,0:21:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}we will convince her{\i0}\N{\i1}to publish a retraction{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.40,0:21:13.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and restore your family's reputation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.36,0:21:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All will be well again, I promise you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.70,0:21:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My dear Lady Bridgerton…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.12,0:21:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is this not a dreadful circumstance,{\i0}\N{\i1}for us both to have been so duped{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.66,0:21:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}by that scheming hussy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.50,0:21:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To think that Miss Thompson{\i0}\N{\i1}would take advantage of my kindness{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.79,0:21:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}after I opened my home to her.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.13,0:21:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You must believe,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.34,0:21:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had no idea of--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.72,0:21:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Featherington,{\i0}\N{\i1}I must ask you to leave.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.77,0:21:46.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-But I have an invitation.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Not anymore.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.39,0:21:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am sure you wish to avoid{\i0}\N{\i1}any further unpleasantness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.75,0:22:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-That should teach them.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Lady Cowper snickers]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.21,0:22:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Teach them what, Miss Cowper?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.58,0:22:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Judging not, lest we too be judged?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.89,0:22:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.86,0:22:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Something troubles you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.53,0:22:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know you are a grown woman now,{\i0}\N{\i1}but I am still your mother,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.32,0:22:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you can come to me{\i0}\N{\i1}when you need advice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.29,0:22:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marriage has its joys,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.20,0:22:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but it also brings with it{\i0}\N{\i1}its special trials.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.92,0:22:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In that, you are correct.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.79,0:22:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My marriage is far from perfect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.63,0:22:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, then, share your thoughts.{\i0}\N{\i1}Perhaps I can offer my wisdom.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.47,0:23:01.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or perhaps you will send me off{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.26,0:23:03.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with more vague metaphors{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.47,0:23:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and trite remarks.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.51,0:23:06.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Darling, I--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.43,0:23:08.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am… merely trying to be of help.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.81,0:23:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you know{\i0}\N{\i1}what might have truly helped matters?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.98,0:23:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If your motherly advice{\i0}\N{\i1}had actually prepared me to wed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.53,0:23:19.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Whatever do you mean?{\i0}\N{\i1}-I mean you sent me out into the world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.86,0:23:21.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}no better than a fool.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.57,0:23:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You taught me how to play pretend,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.12,0:23:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but nothing{\i0}\N{\i1}of the realities of married life,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.45,0:23:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of marital relations.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.29,0:23:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you had informed me about the things{\i0}\N{\i1}that were truly important,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.71,0:23:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if I'd have known the truth,{\i0}\N{\i1}then perhaps I--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.39,0:23:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.27,0:23:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is the heat.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.15,0:23:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duchess is quite overcome.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.32,0:24:09.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We were ridiculed by all today,{\i0}\N{\i1}treated as though we were worthless,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.12,0:24:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and it's all your fault.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.33,0:24:11.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How could I have been at fault?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.50,0:24:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was not even there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.92,0:24:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If it were not for your habit,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.75,0:24:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}we'd have been able{\i0}\N{\i1}to rid ourselves of Miss Thompson{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.84,0:24:19.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the moment we learned of her condition.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.92,0:24:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[shakily] None of this{\i0}\N{\i1}would have happened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.51,0:24:23.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My lady.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.30,0:24:25.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Duchess of Hastings…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.97,0:24:26.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.81,0:24:40.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am so glad{\i0}\N{\i1}you thought to visit us, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.36,0:24:42.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I fear your mother was rather heated{\i0}\N{\i1}at the luncheon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.99,0:24:46.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But of course,{\i0}\N{\i1}if you have come to offer an explanation…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.78,0:24:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I require a word with Miss Thompson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.58,0:24:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.62,0:24:54.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.08,0:24:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For what it is worth, I am sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.29,0:25:01.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your brother is a sweet boy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.09,0:25:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not need to--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.88,0:25:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales sharply]{\i0}\N{\i1}I came here to apologize to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.09,0:25:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.01,0:25:11.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I misjudged you, and I wanted to tell you{\i0}\N{\i1}that what you felt you had to do…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.60,0:25:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.39,0:25:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wish it had not happened this way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.60,0:25:18.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are certainly not the only one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.27,0:25:22.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}George was a soldier…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.49,0:25:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but he was also gentle and kind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.70,0:25:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was perfect.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.20,0:25:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I fancied myself in love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.87,0:25:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The next thing I knew, my courses stopped,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.92,0:25:41.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I found myself with child, and…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.13,0:25:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.89,0:25:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.84,0:25:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is Sir George's surname?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.14,0:25:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or do you know{\i0}\N{\i1}where he is stationed, his regiment?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.81,0:25:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Whatever for, Your Grace?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.02,0:26:00.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hear General Langham{\i0}\N{\i1}and his wife are in London.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.27,0:26:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps I could speak to him or her{\i0}\N{\i1}and have…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.78,0:26:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}have Sir George found.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.24,0:26:08.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What use would that be?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.61,0:26:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}George does not want to be with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.99,0:26:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But do you really want to be alone?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.49,0:26:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No rank, no protection,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.91,0:26:17.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}no support for you or your child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.21,0:26:20.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Surely anything is better than that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.38,0:26:23.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why should he be the one{\i0}\N{\i1}to choose your future{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.88,0:26:26.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}when he clearly cares not for the outcome?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.55,0:26:28.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is at fault here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.30,0:26:32.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps I can make him come back…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.93,0:26:35.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and take responsibility{\i0}\N{\i1}for you and his child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.60,0:26:41.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why should you be left all alone{\i0}\N{\i1}to bear the punishment for his crime?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.90,0:26:45.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You truly think you can do this?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.48,0:26:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I assure you, Miss Thompson…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.15,0:26:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am quite capable{\i0}\N{\i1}of doing more than you think.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.93,0:27:14.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have defeated the best, and{\i0}\N{\i1}I'm confident I shall continue to do so.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.51,0:27:15.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.47,0:27:20.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is an appetite for my exhibitions,{\i0}\N{\i1}but they are expensive, which is why--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.44,0:27:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am not here to invest.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.23,0:27:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have a more lucrative proposition{\i0}\N{\i1}in mind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.19,0:27:27.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Say, for you and I{\i0}\N{\i1}to come to some arrangement…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.74,0:27:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}as to the outcome of your next fight?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.91,0:27:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sorry{\i0}\N{\i1}to have taken your time, my lord,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.83,0:27:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I think you would be wise to leave.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.16,0:27:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you'd be wise to listen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.62,0:27:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you rather stake your fortunes{\i0}\N{\i1}on the outcome of a business scheme,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.92,0:27:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}which may very well fail,{\i0}\N{\i1}or back the sure thing?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.59,0:27:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You agree to throw your next match…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.38,0:27:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I will make such a wager{\i0}\N{\i1}on your opponent{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.59,0:27:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that even half my winnings{\i0}\N{\i1}will set you and your family up for life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.51,0:27:58.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My honor is not for sale.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.23,0:28:03.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[tense music plays]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.78,0:28:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is a reason{\i0}\N{\i1}your backers are dwindling, Mr. Mondrich.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.99,0:28:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're a performer, a mere entertainment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.20,0:28:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We are happy to trade wages{\i0}\N{\i1}on the outcome of your fists,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.46,0:28:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but no gentleman will ever see you{\i0}\N{\i1}as a respectable man of business.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.17,0:28:32.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know you have a fighting spirit…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.97,0:28:36.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}passed down by your father, no doubt.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.01,0:28:38.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was a soldier, yeah?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.01,0:28:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Managed to flee the colonies{\i0}\N{\i1}after serving in Dunmore's regiment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.23,0:28:46.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think he sought his freedom{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.69,0:28:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}all for his future son{\i0}\N{\i1}to become some exhausted fighter,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.86,0:28:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}stumbling into the ring{\i0}\N{\i1}to put food on the table for his family?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.20,0:28:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do not dare speak of my family.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.32,0:28:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathing heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.41,0:28:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.66,0:29:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… I apologize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.62,0:29:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[breathes heavily]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.79,0:29:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I only mean to say, I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.21,0:29:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm doing this for my family too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.71,0:29:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look, one simple arrangement,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.63,0:29:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and both our problems will be solved.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.09,0:29:19.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I merely ask that you have a think on it…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.76,0:29:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at the very least.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.03,0:29:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Rose] The ton has been desperate{\i0}\N{\i1}for you since you returned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.45,0:29:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've been drowning in calling cards.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.37,0:29:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Danbury requires your attendance{\i0}\N{\i1}at her party on Thursday.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.54,0:29:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mm. A collection of married ladies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.13,0:29:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can only imagine{\i0}\N{\i1}the questions they will have for me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.63,0:29:54.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall inform her footman that{\i0}\N{\i1}you are not feeling well from the travel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.55,0:29:56.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.59,0:30:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you suppose the general's wife will be{\i0}\N{\i1}in attendance at Lady Danbury's soiree?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.97,0:30:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mrs. Langham?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.81,0:30:07.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I heard she enjoys society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.44,0:30:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then send word back.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.94,0:30:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would love to attend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.96,0:30:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[boisterous chatter and laughter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.72,0:30:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:48.64,0:30:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Welcome to my den of iniquity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.78,0:31:04.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe you already know{\i0}\N{\i1}Lady Trowbridge, Your Grace,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:04.28,0:31:06.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but have you met Lucy Granville?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.12,0:31:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And this is Kitty Langham.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.12,0:31:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The general's wife, yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.79,0:31:14.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, lovely to meet you all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.50,0:31:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, do not just stare.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.55,0:31:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Deal the duchess in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.13,0:31:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We shall teach you the rules.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.89,0:31:26.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}First, a woman takes her wedding vows,{\i0}\N{\i1}then we gamblers take her virtue.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.89,0:31:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-If her husband has left any to be taken.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[women laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.56,0:31:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Danbury] Have no fear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.44,0:31:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Each turn, all you have to do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.27,0:31:36.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}is set your token on the card{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.90,0:31:39.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you believe the dealer will turn over.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.32,0:31:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, ladies, place your bets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.82,0:31:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Takes away the sting of losing,{\i0}\N{\i1}I rather think.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.24,0:31:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Danbury]{\i0}\N{\i1}The duchess is a quick study.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.16,0:31:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sure she will have{\i0}\N{\i1}the measure of things in no time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:53.37,0:31:57.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All it takes is{\i0}\N{\i1}a little practice and perseverance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:02.43,0:32:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Trowbridge groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.89,0:32:04.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:11.48,0:32:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Evening, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.35,0:32:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's funny meeting you here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:15.98,0:32:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am utterly comical.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.82,0:32:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You've been avoiding me.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Now you are being the jester.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.78,0:32:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you're not avoiding my company,{\i0}\N{\i1}you won't mind if I join you for a drink?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.82,0:32:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[door opens]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.07,0:32:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[indistinct chatter and laughter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.40,0:33:00.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I shall need a large glass.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[waiter] Yes, sir.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.40,0:33:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[excited chatter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.28,0:33:08.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Trowbridge groans]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.66,0:33:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The earl would have my head{\i0}\N{\i1}if he knew how much money I have lost.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.79,0:33:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The earl is but two years old.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.54,0:33:16.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm. Well, then, I'm in luck, am I not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.96,0:33:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[women laughing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.01,0:33:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Seems I have been blessed{\i0}\N{\i1}with some beginner's luck.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.88,0:33:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The game is not over yet, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.26,0:33:30.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.51,0:33:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder, Mrs. Langham--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.64,0:33:34.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Kitty," please.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.18,0:33:36.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have won so much of my money,{\i0}\N{\i1}it is only right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.06,0:33:38.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] Kitty, then.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.52,0:33:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is a soldier in service{\i0}\N{\i1}I am hoping to find for a friend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.86,0:33:45.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think your husband{\i0}\N{\i1}might be able to assist me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.40,0:33:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will have to ask that of him yourself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.86,0:33:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He is so rarely at home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.12,0:33:50.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am so sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.28,0:33:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles] Whatever for?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.95,0:33:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is quite the ideal situation{\i0}\N{\i1}to live a separate life to one's husband.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.54,0:33:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am afforded all the freedoms of marriage{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.54,0:34:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}while bearing none of the burden{\i0}\N{\i1}of his company.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.09,0:34:04.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, what of your children?{\i0}\N{\i1}Do they not miss their father?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.51,0:34:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's difficult to miss{\i0}\N{\i1}someone you've never known.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.09,0:34:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You forget the duchess is still{\i0}\N{\i1}in the first bloom of marriage.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.77,0:34:16.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, the famous love match.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.35,0:34:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Pay me no heed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.19,0:34:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The duke's company, I am sure,{\i0}\N{\i1}is anything but a burden to you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.98,0:34:26.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can tell you where to write. My husband.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.74,0:34:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps the general{\i0}\N<span style="style2">will {\i0}{\i1}grant you a response.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.45,0:34:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not as if you are his wife.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.37,0:34:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.20,0:34:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Duchess, you win again!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.08,0:34:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.71,0:34:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Seeing how you entertain yourself,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.50,0:34:41.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I rather think{\i0}\N{\i1}you the victor, Lady Danbury.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.96,0:34:44.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Kitty laughs]{\i0}\N{\i1}-I rather think so too.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.59,0:34:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:45.51,0:34:46.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.17,0:34:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's a fine color.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.38,0:34:51.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the bubbles…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.81,0:34:54.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[satisfied exhale]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:54.81,0:34:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.27,0:34:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't get me wrong. I love a good brandy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.98,0:35:02.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-But sometimes, nothing'll do but a beer.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Would you just get to the point?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.98,0:35:05.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I don't know what you're talking about.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes, you do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.61,0:35:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're correct. I do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.07,0:35:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just like I know that you've obviously{\i0}\N{\i1}made a considerable error with my sister.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.20,0:35:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How, may I ask, could you infer{\i0}\N{\i1}that {\i0}<span style="style2">I{\i0}{\i1} was the one to make the error?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:14.37,0:35:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, I know my sister quite well.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.95,0:35:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And while she is{\i0}\N{\i1}an unusually capable woman,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.21,0:35:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}she is not capable{\i0}\N{\i1}of fucking up this severely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.59,0:35:27.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you not ever get tired{\i0}\N{\i1}of pretending to be so perfect?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.26,0:35:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Anthony chuckles]{\i0}\N{\i1}-It's exhausting just watching you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.59,0:35:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We may not be perfect,{\i0}\N{\i1}but at least we keep our promises.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.97,0:35:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know nothing of my commitments.{\i0}\N{\i1}I'm trying to be a man of my word.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.76,0:35:35.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am trying to keep--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.01,0:35:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.72,0:35:41.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I wouldn't expect you to understand.{\i0}\N{\i1}-What do you mean by that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.27,0:35:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I mean that you leave{\i0}\N{\i1}a litany of broken promises{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.69,0:35:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}behind you everywhere you go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.19,0:35:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your duty to protect Daphne{\i0}\N{\i1}from Nigel Berbrooke?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.44,0:35:48.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What about your own reckless affairs,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.99,0:35:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}seeing that opera singer{\i0}\N{\i1}you believe no one knows about?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:51.20,0:35:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You judge me,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.11,0:35:54.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}yet you can't understand{\i0}\N{\i1}the responsibility of heading a family,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.82,0:35:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because you've never had one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.20,0:35:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But Daphne is my family now,{\i0}\N{\i1}and there is no changing that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.79,0:36:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though it is most unfortunate{\i0}\N{\i1}that I shall never quite reach{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.83,0:36:03.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the lofty ideal you have demonstrated.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.75,0:36:07.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is most unfortunate is the fact{\i0}\N{\i1}that your father was so absent,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.21,0:36:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}he never gave you a proper example{\i0}\N{\i1}of how to lead a household.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.68,0:36:23.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well,{\i0}\N{\i1}you certainly make it look difficult.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.44,0:36:27.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I beg your pardon?{\i0}\N{\i1}-With your constant struggles.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.94,0:36:29.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You cannot manage it, can you?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Hastings--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.65,0:36:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your responsibility.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.11,0:36:32.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You, fulfilling the promise{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.78,0:36:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that every firstborn son makes{\i0}\N{\i1}to his father before he dies.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.07,0:36:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony exhales deeply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.99,0:36:41.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Do you think{\i0}\N{\i1}he is looking down on you now, ashamed?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.08,0:36:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mortified at what you have done?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.08,0:36:47.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder,{\i0}\N{\i1}what would the former viscount say?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.59,0:36:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony roars]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.30,0:36:52.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.51,0:36:55.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Anthony roars]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:58.89,0:37:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[man 1] Calm down! Get off him!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.10,0:37:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[indistinct yelling]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[man 2] Calm down!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.73,0:37:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[man 1] Get off!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.27,0:37:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Anthony grunting]{\i0}\N{\i1}-[Simon panting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.42,0:37:29.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Simon sighs softly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:40.35,0:37:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It seems I became a little too rough{\i0}\N{\i1}training with Will.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:53.15,0:37:55.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Shall I call for Jeffries?{\i0}\N{\i1}-No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.70,0:38:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.58,0:38:04.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}With four brothers,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.70,0:38:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you cannot imagine the nasty cuts{\i0}\N{\i1}I have tended to over the years. [laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.68,0:38:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[inhales sharply, grunts]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.52,0:38:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[soft music playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.05,0:39:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why will you not unfold yourself to me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.77,0:39:06.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Daphne…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.69,0:39:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A child would be a blessing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:21.78,0:39:23.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell me why you are so adamant.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.57,0:39:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I swore a long time ago{\i0}\N{\i1}that I would never sire a child.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:27.66,0:39:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.66,0:39:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My father…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:33.79,0:39:37.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}cared more about the continuation{\i0}\N{\i1}of the Hastings line…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.13,0:39:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than anything in the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.34,0:39:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}More than my mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.47,0:39:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}More than me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.89,0:39:50.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And so I made a vow{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.31,0:39:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that his efforts would be in vain…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.90,0:39:58.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that the line would die with me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.07,0:40:05.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So this is all…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.33,0:40:08.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because of a vow?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.83,0:40:15.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You made a vow to me too. Or…{\i0}\N{\i1}Or has our wedding day slipped your mind?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.75,0:40:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I told you--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.67,0:40:20.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You told me{\i0}\N{\i1}that you could not {\i0}<span style="style2">have {\i0}{\i1}children.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:21.09,0:40:24.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You did not tell me it was some--{\i0}\N{\i1}some token of revenge{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.80,0:40:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}against a man{\i0}\N{\i1}who no longer walks this earth.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:27.10,0:40:29.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I swore to him on his deathbed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.31,0:40:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you betrayed me in our marriage bed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.07,0:40:41.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let me be certain I understand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:42.95,0:40:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will neither have children,{\i0}\N{\i1}nor the happiness we could have together,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.83,0:40:50.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}because you promised{\i0}\N{\i1}your father you would not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.91,0:40:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.83,0:40:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne] Say it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:55.33,0:40:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Say it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.33,0:40:58.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It cannot be undone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:02.05,0:41:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I thank you{\i0}\N{\i1}for your elucidation, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.09,0:41:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If your hatred for your father outweighs{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.80,0:41:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}any affection{\i0}\N{\i1}that you might bear towards me…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:12.64,0:41:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}then you are right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.14,0:41:16.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It cannot be undone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.31,0:41:20.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My courses are due{\i0}\N{\i1}within the next few days.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.61,0:41:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will know then{\i0}\N{\i1}which vow you have broken,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.94,0:41:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and how we are to spend{\i0}\N{\i1}the rest of our lives,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.49,0:41:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}miserable together…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:29.24,0:41:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}or perfectly happy apart.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.63,0:41:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Dearest reader, a question.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.50,0:41:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is anything more exhilarating{\i0}\N{\i1}than taking a gamble?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.34,0:41:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For it is often the highest risk{\i0}\N{\i1}that carries the greatest reward.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.81,0:42:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet, wager wrongly,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.77,0:42:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and you might find yourself left{\i0}\N{\i1}with nothing but regret.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.99,0:42:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Ensure it is delivered to this address.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.45,0:42:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">Of course, one can never know for sure{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:13.49,0:42:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}whether a wager{\i0}\N{\i1}will make a fortune or ruin it,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.12,0:42:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}unless one chooses a more secure pursuit.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:23.80,0:42:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But as the season continues,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.38,0:42:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the biggest gamblers{\i0}\N{\i1}have yet to truly show their hand…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.76,0:42:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}which leaves gossip{\i0}\N{\i1}in short supply in recent days.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.72,0:42:40.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In fact, this author can think{\i0}\N{\i1}of no other event that merits a mention.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.44,0:42:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}"No other event."{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:43.82,0:42:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But my luncheon.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.78,0:42:48.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}At least she did not say anything odious.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:49.20,0:42:50.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is far worse.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.45,0:42:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She wrote nothing.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:01.50,0:43:04.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Lady Whistledown]{\i0}\N<span style="style2">It is worthy of note, however,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:04.84,0:43:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that the Duke and Duchess of Hastings{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:07.13,0:43:09.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}have yet to entertain callers together.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.72,0:43:17.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Our newlyweds are no doubt still secluded{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.68,0:43:20.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}in nuptial bliss.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.48,0:43:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who could fault them?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.98,0:43:26.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And who could be surprised{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.57,0:43:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}if their diligent efforts are rewarded{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:29.82,0:43:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with a new arrival within the year?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.59,0:43:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In the past, every Whistledown revelation{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:47.96,0:43:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}appeared to be plucked{\i0}\N{\i1}from a public event,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:50.17,0:43:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}where any of our ton{\i0}\N{\i1}could have borne witness.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:52.01,0:43:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But the column{\i0}\N{\i1}that singled out Marina was different.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.05,0:43:54.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was personal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:55.01,0:43:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your mama did not just help Marina{\i0}\N{\i1}hide her condition all on her own.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.72,0:43:59.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course not.{\i0}\N{\i1}Every servant in our household knew.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.85,0:44:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A servant is unlikely.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.85,0:44:05.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, perhaps a tradesperson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.65,0:44:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someone who visited{\i0}\N{\i1}your household regularly{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.11,0:44:09.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}might have seen or overheard something.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.99,0:44:10.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a possibility.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:10.99,0:44:13.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In that case, we must reconsider{\i0}\N{\i1}our methods of inquiry to this end.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.37,0:44:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is wonderful, Pen.{\i0}\N{\i1}I must tell the queen of our new theory.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.41,0:44:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then tell her at tonight's concert.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:22.62,0:44:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I know you are not yet out,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.96,0:44:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I am sure your mama{\i0}\N{\i1}would still allow you to attend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.46,0:44:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Once we unmask Whistledown--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.17,0:44:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, yes,{\i0}\N{\i1}the Featherington honor will be restored.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.30,0:44:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I must return home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:32.93,0:44:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I shall take the back stairs{\i0}\N{\i1}so no one will see me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.76,0:44:36.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And, El?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:37.97,0:44:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.10,0:44:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wrote to General Langham,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.15,0:44:48.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I have told him all about Sir George.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.44,0:44:49.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If he is a man of honor--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:49.57,0:44:52.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You wrote to the general?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:52.19,0:44:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And did the duke{\i0}\N{\i1}sign his name as well on this letter?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.32,0:44:58.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.12,0:44:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}no.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:00.74,0:45:01.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But--{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.75,0:45:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina, what is it?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:05.83,0:45:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The general will not concern himself{\i0}\N{\i1}to write back to you, Your Grace.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:10.09,0:45:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You do not know that.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.72,0:45:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He will pay attention{\i0}\N{\i1}to the words of a duchess.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:15.05,0:45:16.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He must.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.22,0:45:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you so unworldly?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:18.10,0:45:19.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… I'm sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.01,0:45:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I… Your help is greatly appreciated,{\i0}\N{\i1}but there is nothing more you can do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.39,0:45:26.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Marina--{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is over.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.85,0:45:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have already accepted the fact.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:30.02,0:45:31.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank you for your efforts.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.91,0:45:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.20,0:45:44.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Missing the concert?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Indeed.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:45.12,0:45:47.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not exactly in the mood{\i0}\N{\i1}for music and finery this evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:52.50,0:45:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want to apologize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.47,0:46:00.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are there locusts in the streets?{\i0}\N{\i1}Blood in the Thames?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:00.26,0:46:01.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are the end of days upon us already?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:01.89,0:46:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I may have been a trifle harsh with you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.31,0:46:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I'm sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.56,0:46:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You merely wished to protect me{\i0}\N{\i1}from my more…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.40,0:46:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}foolish impulses.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.57,0:46:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So you admit it now?{\i0}\N{\i1}You were acting a fool?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:13.57,0:46:16.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-As apologies go, this is certainly novel.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Hush, you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.20,0:46:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Colin chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.62,0:46:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You may hurt now, but the pain will pass.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.24,0:46:24.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have the love of all your family{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.70,0:46:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and the honor of your actions.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.75,0:46:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Soon you will forget Miss Thompson's name,{\i0}\N{\i1}and it will-- [sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:32.67,0:46:34.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It will be{\i0}\N{\i1}as if you never loved her at all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.96,0:46:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And how have these precepts served you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.72,0:46:41.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Aside from being{\i0}\N{\i1}the most dismal, troubling ones{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.68,0:46:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've heard in quite some time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.14,0:46:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's a work in progress, to be sure.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.27,0:46:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[both chuckle]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.31,0:46:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose I was surprised to hear{\i0}\N{\i1}you wished to join us this evening.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.31,0:46:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I suppose I must be grateful{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.69,0:46:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}for your restraint{\i0}\N{\i1}in not using any feathers.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.78,0:46:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Violet laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.86,0:46:57.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-You look lovely.{\i0}\N{\i1}-Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.36,0:47:00.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eloise… [sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.41,0:47:08.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Taking your place in society should be{\i0}\N{\i1}an exciting time in a young woman's life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.46,0:47:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are not truly ready,{\i0}\N{\i1}I shall not ask you to play pretend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.46,0:47:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps I have been rushing you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.46,0:47:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We need not hasten your coming out{\i0}\N{\i1}before you feel prepared.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.22,0:47:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The queen will be in attendance{\i0}\N{\i1}at tonight's concert, will she not?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.44,0:47:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believe she will.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.86,0:47:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then I am looking forward to it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:34.61,0:47:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}An exciting time indeed, Mama.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:58.88,0:47:59.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you ready?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.84,0:48:01.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.64,0:48:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[guests chattering]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.89,0:48:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[violin quintet playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:21.90,0:48:24.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[indistinct chatter]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.54,0:48:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Excuse me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.50,0:48:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sir Granville.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.84,0:48:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Bridgerton.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:39.55,0:48:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sorry.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.09,0:48:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Excuse us.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.55,0:48:46.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would simply like to understand your…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.18,0:48:50.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}situation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.43,0:48:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Henry sighs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.77,0:48:54.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-I would just like to understand.{\i0}\N{\i1}-It is simple.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:55.27,0:48:57.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am in love with Lord Wetherby.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.11,0:48:58.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're married.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:58.48,0:49:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And our marriage affords my wife{\i0}\N{\i1}her freedoms and protections.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:01.74,0:49:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is a happier union{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:02.90,0:49:05.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}than most of the people in this room have,{\i0}\N{\i1}I assure you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.49,0:49:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What is the advantage for the young ladies{\i0}\N{\i1}Lord Wetherby is courting?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.37,0:49:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Do they also share this understanding?{\i0}\N{\i1}-[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.62,0:49:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What about honor? Romance?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.04,0:49:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What would you know of either?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.79,0:49:18.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We live under constant threat of danger.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:18.79,0:49:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I risk my life every day for love.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:24.80,0:49:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You have no idea what it is like{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:26.59,0:49:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to be in a room{\i0}\N{\i1}with someone you cannot live without…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.10,0:49:33.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and yet still feel{\i0}\N{\i1}as though you are oceans apart.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:33.73,0:49:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stealing your glances,{\i0}\N{\i1}disguising your touches.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.94,0:49:38.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We cannot so much as smile at each other…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.94,0:49:42.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}without first ensuring{\i0}\N{\i1}no one else is watching.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.36,0:49:46.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It takes courage…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.07,0:49:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to live outside{\i0}\N{\i1}the traditional expectations of society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:52.62,0:49:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You talk of doing the same…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:55.87,0:49:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but perhaps it is merely just that…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:00.09,0:50:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}all talk.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.89,0:50:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And so you see,{\i0}\N{\i1}Your Majesty, it is clear as day.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:15.39,0:50:18.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Lady Whistledown works closely{\i0}\N{\i1}with the members of the ton,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.56,0:50:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}yet she is not a member herself.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:20.27,0:50:22.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She is a tradesperson.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.73,0:50:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that all?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.19,0:50:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I beg your pardon?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:27.24,0:50:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I am no longer in need of your services.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:30.32,0:50:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But, uh… my theory…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:32.62,0:50:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It is not necessary.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:33.91,0:50:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have hired a team of Bow Street Runners{\i0}\N{\i1}to do a proper investigation.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.42,0:50:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They will unmask Whistledown,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:40.08,0:50:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and she shall be made to pay{\i0}\N{\i1}for her impertinence.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.67,0:50:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That noxious gossip rag…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.42,0:50:48.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}will finally cease to exist.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.47,0:50:50.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You want to silence her?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.97,0:50:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-But there is still good she must do.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[scoffs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.43,0:50:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Child, go.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.48,0:51:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-How long is this concert?{\i0}\N{\i1}-Three hours?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:06.40,0:51:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[groans]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Four?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.94,0:51:10.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, uh,{\i0}\N{\i1}I certainly have already heard enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.07,0:51:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You are my most favorite brother.{\i0}\N{\i1}Do you know that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.98,0:51:42.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[horses neigh]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.69,0:51:49.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[clears throat]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:50.61,0:51:53.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I would like to make a stop{\i0}\N{\i1}and pick up a friend.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.12,0:51:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A friend?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.83,0:51:57.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I not have a friend?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.24,0:51:58.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Eloise chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:58.66,0:52:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm not bound by the rules of society.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.54,0:52:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-Please do not tell Mother.{\i0}\N{\i1}-[scoffs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.05,0:52:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why are we at the modiste?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.31,0:52:18.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[shop door closes]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.81,0:52:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mademoiselle Bridgerton!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.86,0:52:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is my sister, Eloise,{\i0}\N{\i1}and we will be dropping her at home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.87,0:52:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Benedict] Mm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.37,0:52:43.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Genevieve] Hmm.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.50,0:52:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How… How was your night, {\i0}<span style="style2">ma chérie{\i0}{\i1}?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:50.76,0:52:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:52.34,0:52:53.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}everything I expected.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:54.13,0:52:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Horrible and terribly boring.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:56.22,0:52:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[chuckles]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.26,0:53:01.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So this is why you do not wish{\i0}\N{\i1}to lower your hems? [laughs]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:03.02,0:53:04.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The entire ton were there,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:04.14,0:53:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and I did not have{\i0}\N{\i1}a single worthwhile exchange.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.73,0:53:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The entire ton?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:07.86,0:53:10.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You mean,{\i0}\N{\i1}everyone except for the Featheringtons?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.78,0:53:13.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}-[Genevieve laughs]{\i0}\N{\i1}-Yes, everyone except…{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:14.74,0:53:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}them.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.74,0:53:20.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Your mama did not just help Marina{\i0}\N{\i1}hide her condition on her own.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:20.37,0:53:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course not.{\i0}\N{\i1}Every servant in our household knew.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.58,0:53:24.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though, perhaps a tradesperson?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:24.21,0:53:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I certainly never want to cross the woman.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:26.46,0:53:28.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her word as good as gospel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.18,0:53:38.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is everything well, Eloise?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.72,0:53:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hmm?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.68,0:53:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yeah.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:50.73,0:53:52.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}["The Four Seasons" by Vivaldi playing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:46.37,0:54:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[teapot whistling]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:23.78,0:55:25.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Vivaldi's "Four Seasons" continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.76,0:55:38.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping lightly]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.34,0:55:43.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasps sharply]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.65,0:55:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.44,0:55:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can we talk?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:02.20,0:56:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.24,0:56:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you still awake?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:12.92,0:56:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[shouts] Marina!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:14.54,0:56:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina! Marina!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.67,0:56:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.59,0:56:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mama, make haste!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.01,0:56:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Marina? Marina, I'm here. It's okay.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:23.18,0:56:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Penelope gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:29.52,0:56:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[grunting]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:43.53,0:56:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[gasping, sobbing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.04,0:56:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne gasping]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:58.88,0:57:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crying]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:00.13,0:57:01.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[music ends]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.01,0:57:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Daphne continues crying]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.60,0:57:15.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[sobbing]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.61,0:57:19.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[crying continues]{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.75,0:57:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[instrumental music playing]{\i0}
